  "section_notes": "S1 is strict: all incidents reportable within 24h, customer notice within 24h, no cause-uncertainty exemption. S2 sets 55°C and a 5% corrective-action threshold but no sales suspension, while giving purchasers numeric failure rates (not public). S3 and S4 accept 6-year retrofit and 36-month suppression, respecting NW-2 and HC-2; S5 has a mandatory 8/100k recall trigger with no transition, which applies to Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) but not Northwind's flagship (6.4)."
